      "description": "Kernels, numerics, and HW/SW co-design for the MLA accelerator family: tiled many-core ASICs with DMA-driven data movement\n\n1. Roofline-Level LLM Kernels\n1) Invented auto-split, an adaptive search that partitions tensors and generates layouts automatically (US 12,639,056, sole inventor)\n2) Based on auto-split, set roofline for the latency of any model in 1 second\n\n2. Performance Modeling and Root-Cause Analysis\n1) Built analytical prefill/decode phase of all LLMs\n2) Identified synchronization freezes between instruction and data queues as the limiter of effective bandwidth\n\n3. Low-Precision Numerics\n1) Characterized weight quantization: Llama 2 from +0.21% (8-bit) to -4% (4-bit) perplexity change\n2) Designed INT8 KV-cache quantization with little impact on metrics (ARC-easy, ARC-challenge, HellaSwag, MMLU); INV4 KV-cache with acceptable metrics\n\n4. Kernel Authoring Framework and Compiler\n1) Wrote large matrix multiplication in LLM with TOPS efficiency ≥ 90%\n2) Built the LLModel Builder, a composable kernel framework that generates any LLM; extending it to ViT encoders\n3) Invented on-chip data transfers (US 12,260,253, sole inventor); one of fundamental building blocks in a compiler and the Model Builder\n4) Developed light-attention without DRAM access\n5) Fused MLP of any intermediate-size without\tDRAM access\n\n5. Pre-Silicon Development and HW/SW Co-design\n1) Multicast weights\n2) INT8 convolution of bfloat16s\n3) On-chip instruction buffer with (broadcast, loop) ≤ 128kb even for LLM\n4) Deformable convolutions\n5) Grid-sample\n\n6. Software Mitigations for Hardware Limits\n1) lookup-table-based approximation of all non-linear activations without a drop in accuracy\n2) Wrote Grid-Sample, Gather, and TopK without HW support",
