   {
    "title": "ADAPTIVE SEARCH-BASED ALLOCATION OF COMPUTATIONS TO SYNCHRONIZED, INTERCONNECTED PROCESSING ELEMENTS FOR IMPLEMENTING MACHINE LEARNING NETWORKS",
    "issuer": "US 12,639,056 B2 · Issued May 26, 2026",
    "issueDate": {},
    "description": "ABSTRACT\nA system for compiling a machine learning network for execution on a plurality of interconnected processing ele- ments performs the following. tI selects splits (P„Q,,K,) for individual layers of the machine learning network based on\n(a) costs of data transfer between processing elements assuming that inputs and outputs of individual layers have a same spatial split (P,,Q,), and (b) costs of data transfer between processing elements resulting from differences in the spatial splits for inputs and outputs of individual layers. that haven i sales phe asme pie e n energet computer program that allocates computations for executing the machine learning network ot the processing elements according to the selected splits for the individual layers."
   },
   {
    "title": "LAYOUT-BASED DATA TRANSFER BETWEEN SYNCHRONIZED, INTERCONNECTED PROCESSING ELEMENTS FOR IMPLEMENTING MACHINE LEARNING NETWORKS",
    "issuer": "US-12260253-B2 · Issued Mar 25, 2025",
    "issueDate": {},
    "description": "** ABSTRACT **\n\nA machine learning accelerator (MLA) implements a machine learning network (MLN) by using data transfer instructions that coordinate concurrent data transfers between processing elements. Acompiler receives a descrip- tion of a machine learning network and generates the computer program that implements the MLN. The computer program contains instructions that will be run on PEs of the MLA. The PEs are connected by data transfer paths that are known to the compiler. The computations performed by the PEs may require data stored at other PEs. The compiler coordinates the data transfers to avoid conflicts and increase parallelism."
   }
